                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp; &amp; C &amp; &amp;  \\
                    \&amp; _\mathllap{\pi_C} \nearrow &amp; &amp; \searrow _\mathrlap{i_C} \\
                    C \otimes D &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; C \oplus D \\
                    \&amp; _\mathllap{\pi_D} \searrow &amp; &amp; \nearrow _\mathrlap{i_D} \\
                    \&amp; &amp; D &amp; &amp;
                    }
            %p
              This coalgebra equalizer is constructed as the largest subcoalgebra of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \otimes D
              contained in the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Vect
              equalizer. But the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Vect
              equalizer is easily seen to be
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              (cf. the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Vect
              coproducts are themselves disjoint), and so the coalgebra equalizer must be
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              as well, concluding the proof.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p Coproducts of coalgebras are stable under pullback.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p Consider the following diagram:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
